1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,681
So hiking has a lot of benefits.
徒步有许多好处。

2
00:00:03,681 --> 00:00:15,401
I am a firm believer that people should get out of the city, that they should find somewhere where they can be in nature and that they should go for regular hikes.
我很相信，人们应当偶尔走出城市，到自然里去，定期徒步。

3
00:00:15,401 --> 00:00:21,231
I think it's good for the mind. I think it's good for the soul, and it's also good exercise.
我觉得这有益身心，也能锻炼身体。

4
00:00:21,241 --> 00:00:33,040
So if you feel stuck in your apartment, if you're stuck in your house and you just want to be happier, I highly suggest that you find somewhere beautiful to go for a hike.
如果觉得总困在家里，想换换心情，老师建议找个漂亮的地方走走。

5
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:36,641
You can come to Canada if you want, but that's a little bit extreme.
想来加拿大也行，不过那有点太夸张了。

6
00:00:36,641 --> 00:00:43,121
I'm sure if you go out outside of your town or city, there's probably a place where you can go for a nice hike.
我想，只要走出所在的城镇，附近大概就有适合徒步的地方。

7
00:00:43,121 --> 00:00:52,001
You can breathe in the fresh air, you can get a little bit of exercise, and when you're done you'll feel mentally and physically refreshed.
可以呼吸新鲜空气，活动一下；结束后，老师觉得身心都很清爽。

8
00:00:52,001 --> 00:00:57,961
So I waited until fall, or what we also call autumn, to make this English lesson about hiking.
所以我等到秋天才来拍这节徒步英语课，秋天还可以说 autumn。

9
00:00:57,961 --> 00:01:05,081
I waited because this is the best time of year in my opinion to go hiking.
因为在我看来，这是全年最适合徒步的时候。

10
00:01:05,081 --> 00:01:09,471
You can see that the leaves have started to change color.
可以看到，树叶已经开始变色了。

11
00:01:09,481 --> 00:01:16,001
You can see red leaves and brown leaves and orange leaves and yellow leaves and still some green leaves.
这里有红叶、棕叶、橙叶、黄叶，也还有一些绿叶。

12
00:01:16,001 --> 00:01:20,320
And there's even leaves on the ground already.
地上甚至已经落了一些叶子。

13
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:26,880
This time of year, this season in my opinion is the best time to go hiking.
在我看来，每年这个季节最适合徒步。

14
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:35,440
The weather is cooler, the views in nature are amazing, and it's just a great time to be out in the forest.
天气更凉爽，自然景色也很美，正适合到森林里走走。

15
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:39,081
So sometimes you go on a hike to see specific things.
有时，徒步是为了去看某个特别的景物。

16
00:01:39,081 --> 00:01:43,281
Sometimes it's just nature, maybe an old tree that fell in the forest.
有时只是去感受自然，比如看看林中倒下的一棵老树。

17
00:01:43,281 --> 00:01:50,000
Maybe along the hiking trail there's a beautiful waterfall. Sorry, there's no waterfalls on this hiking trail.
也可能沿途有漂亮的瀑布，不过这条小径没有。

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,281
But you also might hike to a point where there is a spectacular view.
也可能走到一个有壮丽景色的地点。

19
00:01:56,281 --> 00:01:59,961
Behind me you can see Lake Ontario.
我身后就是安大略湖。

20
00:01:59,961 --> 00:02:08,281
So one of the rewards of this hiking trail is that you can stand here and you can see Lake Ontario.
这条路线带来的一个惊喜，就是能站在这里看到安大略湖。

21
00:02:08,281 --> 00:02:14,201
You can see some of the beautiful fall colors, and you can see the town below.
你能看见美丽的秋色，还有下方的小镇。

22
00:02:14,201 --> 00:02:22,281
So sometimes you go on a hike for a very specific reason because there's just something awesome to see while you're hiking.
所以有时徒步有很具体的目的，因为沿途有特别值得看的东西。

23
00:02:22,281 --> 00:02:28,040
So you do want to be careful when you're hiking. There's always the possibility that something could go wrong.
当然，徒步也需要小心，总有可能出现意外。

24
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:33,681
If you look down here, it's a little bit treacherous to walk along here.
看这里的路面，走起来有点险。

25
00:02:33,681 --> 00:02:42,320
You could twist your ankle, you might slip and fall, and you want want to just be really, really careful so that you don't hurt yourself.
可能扭到脚踝，也可能滑倒，所以要格外小心，避免受伤。

26
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:51,841
In addition, if you look over here, we are walking along the edge of a very sharp drop off.
另外，看看这边，我们正沿着一处陡降坡面的边缘走。

27
00:02:51,841 --> 00:02:59,671
I wouldn't call this a cliff, but you certainly wouldn't want to accidentally slip and fall down here.
这未必算悬崖，但肯定不希望不小心滑到下面。

28
00:02:59,681 --> 00:03:07,121
That would certainly hurt and would not be a good thing to have happen while you're out for a beautiful hike in nature.
那肯定会受伤，也会破坏这趟美好的自然徒步。

29
00:03:07,121 --> 00:03:12,600
So one of the coolest things about this hiking trail is that there is an observation deck.
这条小径很棒的一点是有个观景台。

30
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:22,761
I'm standing on this observation deck because if I show you what's on the other side of the camera I think you'll really enjoy the view.
我现在就在观景台上，相信你也会喜欢镜头另一侧的景色。

31
00:03:22,761 --> 00:03:27,201
So this would be another example of a spectacular view.
这就是另一个壮观景色的例子。

32
00:03:27,201 --> 00:03:37,320
I feel like it's so spectacular I should just stop talking for a few seconds and let you enjoy it.
景色太美了，我想安静几秒，让你也好好看看。

33
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:45,160
Well, thank you so much for watching this English lesson and for coming on a little hike with me.
谢谢你观看这节英语课，也谢谢你陪我走了这一小段路。
